{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203848-is-your-character-an-expy-of-a-popular-character","id":1203848,"title":"Is your character an expy of a popular character?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-06T08:36:15-07:00","id":1203848,"title":"Is your character an expy of a popular character?","content":"<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/Expy\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/Expy</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12378-fma245","name":"FMA245","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T21:07:07-07:00","id":1209886,"title":"","content":"I've done expies of mythic and historic characters before (Orpheus based Zenith Caste, Tesla based Twilight, Julie D'Aubigny based Eclipse), but not expies of pop culture IP characters. I mean... some of them are INFORMED by pop-culture IPs, like I'm considering a Zorro and Batman influenced Dynast who's living a double life as a folk hero fighting the Realm - but considering she's a fox-masked Fire Aspect with warfans, she's not that close beyond some broad strokes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T22:20:47-07:00","id":1209905,"title":"","content":"My sorcerer character got his name and affinity for spiders from one of the characters in Neil Gaiman's <i>Anansi Boys</i>, but it branches off in a pretty different direction.<br /> <br /> One of my players in an old game, though, made no less than <i>three</i> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CaptainErsatz\" target=\"_blank\">Captain Ersatz</a> characters, because one of the other players misinformed him about the nature of the game prior to his playing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-22-2018, 01:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T01:57:44-07:00","id":1209949,"title":"","content":"In the game I ran:<br /> <br /> One guy played a drunken, lecherous, tattooed ex-Immaculate monk with a bit of an anger issue. He'd joined the Immaculate Order to get out of being prosecuted, but kept breaking the rules so they sent him to be a missionary in the Scavenger Lands, where he promptly joined a band of bandits (I assume 108, never checked). He had an extremely heavy staff, probably weighing 62 <i>jin</i>, but sadly it was not a spade.<br /> <br /> Another player has a dragon-riding princess who reaps blood and souls in the name of Adramelch, a forbidden god of flame. Her evil cousin controls her old kingdom (famous for its dragons), so she's now founded a new one, full of sorcerous, tall, fine-featured, white-skinned mages, and a bunch of dragons (more gryffons though, those being much easier to make with sorcery). Sadly, Arms of the Chosen was not yet out, so she does not wield Soulfarer.<br /> <br /> A third has a genetically-engineered super-warrior designed by the God-Emperor of the Djala who was cast into the Wyld by dark forces. He eventually returned to reswear his loyalty to the God-Emperor of the Djala (actually a different guy, but the Wyld was confusing so he assumes the God-Emperor is immortal), and leads 100 genetically-engineered super-Djala who he grows in tubes in his ancient First-Age monastery. They're kind of warrior-monks, and wear white tabards over their heavy armour. He's now been named Warmaster of the Djala, though I suspect Hero-Ur, his number 2, would be very happy to take the job.<br /> <br /> If you get the references, you'll see that the tone of the Expies is very, very different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-22-2018, 05:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T02:04:36-07:00","id":1209952,"title":"","content":"It's interesting how there are degrees of expy-ism. Like, I've never watched Full Metal Alchemist, but one of my fellow players had, and made a character who I believe is partially based on Scar. I looked into the show a bit at that and found out that my characters past is surprisingly close to that of Shou Tucker. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Neither are straight out 'the same character', but looking at them with the appropriate lens... *hums*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T04:15:22-07:00","id":1209978,"title":"","content":"Well, I've had some fun trying to stat the protagonist/Joker from Persona 5 as a Night Solar (without Ars\u00e8ne, but he can be modeled very easily as a spirit familiar).<br /> It was surprisingly easy.<br /> ... now I want to play that character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T05:21:24-07:00","id":1209983,"title":"","content":"I do it a lot with my NPCs though I take less-obvious routes with portraying the characters that sometimes makes the connection less obvious.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is one of my more overt ones.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Knockdown and Breakout in Transformers Prime are one of my all time favourite antagonist duos. I'd naturally make them Alchemicals, right?<br /> <img src=\"https://pre00.deviantart.net/32bc/th/pre/f/2011/170/7/6/tfp__breakdown_and_knockout_by_delgatron-d3jbckr.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Not exactly.<br /> The reasons why I like these characters that have nothing to do with the fact that they turn into cars. In fact there's some great artwork online depicting Transformers characters as humans while still retaining their essence.<br /> <br /> &quot;Doctor in the House~&quot; Knockout<br /> <img src=\"http://i0.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/newsfeed/001/001/108/b08.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> &quot;Never run when you can fight&quot; Breakdown<br /> <img src=\"https://orig00.deviantart.net/e6c0/f/2012/104/0/4/breakdown_by_fayrenpickpocket-d4w3p7r.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Ended up with The Sculptor of Life and Death a narcissistic Daybreak necrosurgeon and his Dusk Caste partner The Falling Hammer of Oblivion. It took moments of hearing Sculptor talk for my players to figure out he was Knockout.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T08:48:06-07:00","id":1210042,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.bolthole.org/gallery/albums/userpics/10053/Dawn_v5cheap.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">...Guilty.</a><br /> <br /> Granted, though, that I usually finish her capsule description with '...if she ran off to join the Black Company rather than picking up the sword.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T10:49:13-07:00","id":1210094,"title":"","content":"I tend not to; if I can see the seams, so to speak, it tends to take me out of the story.<br /> <br /> That said, in games I've run and played in, one player had Dawn's directly inspired by Saitama and Jet Li's character from Unleashed.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, there was a player who couldn't come up with an original name to save her life, and this she gave us Dr. Buffy Summers, Dr. Hermione Granger, and Bilba Bagginzoid the boggan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T14:08:04-07:00","id":1210146,"title":"","content":"In 1e, my group had a lot of expies. Though I find that's pretty natural in new games with unique settings. When you're still trying to wrap your head around Creation as a setting, expies can be a useful mental shortcut.<br /> <br /> By mid-2e, an expy was a rare thing (note the TVTropes definition calls for expies to be deliberate design choices) as we grew more comfortable with the setting and creating unique characters inspired solely by Exalted's setting and plot hooks. Though I'm particularly prone to characters that look like expies but I was completely unaware of the popular character at the time (we had a whole West focused game before One Piece got popular in our social circles that in hindsight looks like One Piece knock-off central).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T04:26:03-08:00","id":1294674,"title":"","content":"I've got a new one.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://pixel.nymag.com/imgs/daily/vulture/2016/10/21/21-westworld-man-in-black.w700.h700.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> I found Westworld's Man in Black really compelling because of how terrifying he must seem to the Hosts. From their perspective he must sound completely insane, talking about the world like it's some mystery that was created for him to unravel. A version of the truth is that he's basically one of the Gentry who enters their world to amuse himself in ways he never could in his own with the most disturbing part being that he seems to consider his actions as in service of a greater good where he liberates everyone from the shackles of their reality.<br /> <br /> The NPC I made also draws upon the Saint of Killers and Randall Flagg for inspiration of what he is, what he can do and what he ultimately wants.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T04:33:14-08:00","id":1294676,"title":"","content":"Since I never get to play and I really want to go all in with Solar Brawl, I have every intention of basically making Goku, complete with Super Saiyan transformation, if I get the chance. Some details with change to fit the campaign.<br /> <br /> More interesting characters can come with me getting to play rather than ST regularly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T05:26:10-08:00","id":1294683,"title":"","content":"My current Eclipse is an Expy of Batman, albeit one where I ask, &quot;What if Batman fabricated Bruce Wayne wholesale?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T05:46:58-08:00","id":1294692,"title":"","content":"My Water Aspect is a bit of a Captain Ahab Expy, though he has a replaced arm rather than leg. His White Whale is also the Lintha rather than any specific beast, cause those demon summoning bastards keep calling up more monsters for him to hunt.<br /> <br /> Other than that I don't use too many, though I do have NPCs use some aspects of popular chatacters. Usually from Blizzard games as well (an Abyssal based off Arthas, a Dynast King Leoric, etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13696-knurlurzhad","name":"Knurlurzhad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13696_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T11:47:27-08:00","id":1295097,"title":"","content":"So far I\u2019ve done characters based on Kamina, Hassan-i Sabbah, and a Spike Spiegel/John Wick hybrid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T11:57:20-08:00","id":1295099,"title":"","content":"Lunar baby cthluhu, Solar Gorilla Grodd+Tarzan<br /> And tried Solar Zod, and ran a GMPC of Solar Yang Xio Long","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T15:05:45-08:00","id":1295133,"title":"","content":"PC- Ronin Chosen of Battles Captain Jack Sparrow. Wherever he goes fights just seem to happen, and boy is he lucky.<br /> <br /> NPC- Earth Aspect Immaculate Monk Daredevil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T08:14:44-07:00","id":1295560,"title":"","content":"The first character I played was pretty much Hellboy-as-Makoma, from the Hellboy story <i>Makoma</i> (or <i>A Tale Told by a Mummy in the New York City Explorers' Club on August 16, 1993</i>), red stone hand and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T14:25:27-07:00","id":1297812,"title":"","content":"I've got a concept in the works with five sidereals and an antagonist. To make them perfect I've included their supernals, if the abilities line up correctly to allow it. <br /> <br /> A Sail-Supernal Journeys with a golden barque that can reshape and resize itself to travel anywhere it's needed, even inside people, if fate dictates it so.<br /> <br /> A Linguistics-supernal Serenity with massive hair and a soothing demeanor who stresses that anything you think is a mistake is good, because it's led you to this, the most perfect of moments.<br /> <br /> A Survival-supernal Battles who adopts all manner of animals and magical creatures after wrestling them into submission.<br /> <br /> A Performance-supernal Secrets who dazzles people with trivia while keeping the true mysteries of the universe safe.<br /> <br /> A Craft-supernal Endings who will do ANYTHING to destroy a false and harmful rumor, no matter how much firedust it takes.<br /> <br /> Together, they have to deal with some malign force that's unmaking important events from the history of Creation. Those who have seen her passage only remember her blood-red robes and massive, face-concealing red hat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24023-bestcasesurvival","name":"BestCaseSurvival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24023_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T14:49:08-07:00","id":1297817,"title":"","content":"There's been no indication that Sidereals will have Supernal Abilities, or that Craft is being moved into Endings; moreover, how is Carmen Sandiego traveling through time when even the heights of sorcery don't allow for it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T18:14:54-07:00","id":1297840,"title":"","content":"I try not to make characters that are expies. I just want to be creative on my own<br /> <br /> Then realize the OC I just made is just Samuel L Jackson again....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T20:35:11-07:00","id":1297871,"title":"","content":"Just started a new game. This one's something between Sherlock Holmes, Leone Abacchio and O-Ren Ishii","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T23:56:19-07:00","id":1297896,"title":"","content":"The Sidereal NPC circle in my last game were the main characters from My Little Pony... (excepto for Rarity: she was a Goddess in the Bureau of Destiny and their Supervisor, and never appeared in the game)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T06:47:49-07:00","id":1297945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203848-is-your-character-an-expy-of-a-popular-character?p=1297817#post1297817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's been no indication that Sidereals will have Supernal Abilities, or that Craft is being moved into Endings; moreover, how is Carmen Sandiego traveling through time when even the heights of sorcery don't allow for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Replace 'supernal' with 'they have a lot of it' then, since if there are no supernals than caste vs favored doesn't matter. How would you make Adam Savage as a Siddie?<br /> <br /> Not moving through time - unmaking things <i>now. </i>It's a subtle distinction, but I think it's close enough to what I've picked up on as the remit of Getimians that I'll be able to fix it when the rules come out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24023-bestcasesurvival","name":"BestCaseSurvival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24023_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T06:55:36-07:00","id":1297947,"title":"","content":"None of my most recent characters have been, but I shamelessly steal from media for NPCs all the time.<br /> <br /> I also find it a very useful tool for helping people make their daunting first steps into Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T07:32:42-07:00","id":1297952,"title":"","content":"One of the players in my modern game deliberately based his character off Harry Dresden. It was his first Exalted game, we were spitballing character ideas, and he was rather pleased at how well the system supported having &quot;Wizard PI&quot; as a character concept, so he just went with it. <br /> <br /> As for me, I asked myself, &quot;What if Mrs Tiggy-Winkle from the Beatrix Potter tales was an ancient Lunar sorceress?&quot; And then I made it happen because I was the ST and no one could stop me. She's a kindly old lady who likes baking and sewing and who firmly believes that there are few problems in life that don't look better after a good cup of tea. For everything else, there's magma kraken. Eat your vegetables.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T08:00:20-07:00","id":1297956,"title":"","content":"Not myself, but I'm prepping a new Lunar game, and the PCs I've been sent include Gorilla-Tarzan and Druss the Slayer-Walrus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T08:22:12-07:00","id":1297960,"title":"","content":"I've never really done that for other systems that I can recall, but the last Exalted campaign I played in, I played a Chiaroscuran Night Caste based on Dave Strider, with shades of Batman. My ST also read Homestuck, and loosely based his immediate family on Dave's relatives. It was a good (and anxious) time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T08:23:00-07:00","id":1298333,"title":"","content":"I GM and have caved to my desire for referential touchstones with NPCs on occasion. Most egregious at least as far as barely bothering to reskin though was looting Super Kami Guru to be an ancient, half mad Terrestrial occultist and clan leader who nobody can tell if he is some kind of beast man, wyld touched plant man, or of a demon bloodline.<br /> <br /> Usually it is a lot more subtle, I swear!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T11:44:36-07:00","id":1298687,"title":"","content":"My current Lunar started off as a Prince Sidon expy, but as with many of these characters has evolved into his own place. Though now he's dangerously close to turning into Aquaman (a joke that ended in us all agreeing he has the general physical build of Jason Momoa)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23912-scottsman","name":"Scottsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T08:56:38-07:00","id":1299228,"title":"","content":"I've definitely done this a few times. The most recent obvious candidate is The Seer of Pure Imagination, a Craft Supernal Twilight who makes weird magical candies and a variety of other strange things by harnessing a little of the Wyld. I wish I'd gotten to build him right and play him more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11006-bowerbird","name":"Bowerbird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11006_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T08:03:21-07:00","id":1299600,"title":"","content":"I want to talk about an expy I never got to use.<br /> <br /> Edward Cullen as an Abyssal. You see my group used to include a World of Darkness player who would've absolutely relished putting Edward Cullen's head on a spike, I'm careful about having cameo that exists just for &quot;you suck and we hate you&quot; but on this one I was inspired.<br /> <br /> Essentially I was going to play the Twilight vampire 100% straight and have him try and lure in one of the female NPCs moving towards her with predatory intent as his alabaster skin sparkles in the sun. He would've had some custom charms off Dread Lord's Demeanour that let him grapple someone with a mere look so his would be vctim is at once entralled and rooted in fear like a terrified animal. When the player characters become involved they find he's fast, he's strong and that skin as hard as stone. He's creepy with his dialogue too and proud to be the ultimate predator.<br /> <br /> His death is almost Rasputin like and nothing short of incinerating his remains is sufficient confirmation that he's finally dead.<br /> <br /> Problem was when 2e ended he switched out his Lunar for a Dawn Caste who had this ill-defined hate for Abyssals that stemmed from his homeland's problems with its undead neighbours (there was no Deathlord on the scene, just undead warlords feuding over their lost empire) and didn't really seem to like anyone enough to perform a heroic rescue, we never really ironed out the problems with the character and he eventually left the game. Hence Edward Cullen Abyssal never came to pass. Probably for the best, but it could've been fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T10:09:31-07:00","id":1299641,"title":"","content":"Closest I've come really was starting the seed of a Twilight character based off The Village Blacksmith from Longfellow's poem; my characters tend to be very archetypal, but not expies of anyone in particular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T07:47:05-07:00","id":1299949,"title":"","content":"Haven't actually played t his character yet, but I have an Abyssal Antagonist concept based on Sister Friede from Dark Souls III","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T17:23:06-07:00","id":1300709,"title":"","content":"My first Exalted character, a 1e Chosen of Battles, was yoinked straight from Dynasty Warriors. Their take on Zhou Yu. And one of my 2e Infernal NPCs was basically Cataphract Mussolini.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Known elsewhere as Kurulham. Void where permitted.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/s/d34vnu2hx0ifmk5/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4277-jackson-mackenzie","name":"Jackson MacKenzie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T18:40:53-07:00","id":1300994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203848-is-your-character-an-expy-of-a-popular-character?p=1299600#post1299600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to talk about an expy I never got to use.<br /> <br /> Edward Cullen as an Abyssal. You see my group used to include a World of Darkness player who would've absolutely relished putting Edward Cullen's head on a spike, I'm careful about having cameo that exists just for &amp;quot;you suck and we hate you&amp;quot; but on this one I was inspired.<br /> <br /> Essentially I was going to play the Twilight vampire 100% straight and have him try and lure in one of the female NPCs moving towards her with predatory intent as his alabaster skin sparkles in the sun. He would've had some custom charms off Dread Lord's Demeanour that let him grapple someone with a mere look so his would be vctim is at once entralled and rooted in fear like a terrified animal. When the player characters become involved they find he's fast, he's strong and that skin as hard as stone. He's creepy with his dialogue too and proud to be the ultimate predator.<br /> <br /> His death is almost Rasputin like and nothing short of incinerating his remains is sufficient confirmation that he's finally dead.<br /> <br /> Problem was when 2e ended he switched out his Lunar for a Dawn Caste who had this ill-defined hate for Abyssals that stemmed from his homeland's problems with its undead neighbours (there was no Deathlord on the scene, just undead warlords feuding over their lost empire) and didn't really seem to like anyone enough to perform a heroic rescue, we never really ironed out the problems with the character and he eventually left the game. Hence Edward Cullen Abyssal never came to pass. Probably for the best, but it could've been fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in Exalted, but in Aeon Trinity (1st edition) one of my players did this and while showing off for the female character he wanted to impress got himself killed and his face permanently tattooed on the hind end of another player. <br /> <br /> I rarely get to play as a player and usually am the storyteller and many of the npc that I use are characters from another medium usually books.<br /> In Exalted I have used Pennywise from It. <br /> B.A. Barracus from the A-Team<br /> Stonewall Jackson<br /> Custer<br /> Harry Potter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T10:37:45-07:00","id":1305081,"title":"","content":"all of my characters have basis behind them from some character or another, but i tend to change them enough that its hard to tell. honestly though the best are when the expy is unintentional and i just ran with it. in 2e one of the first characters i made was a very short lived ghost-blooded (HA). she was originally supposed to be based on youmu konpaku, from Touhou, (admittedly). the only thing i could find that would be an outright buff to her weilding 2 swords was fire dragon style. so i gave her that (made up some story how her father was a disgraced immaculate monk who began to travel the world). anyways she eventually became Annie from league of legends. and then i ditched her swords... in hindsight the character was fated to die. i went too deep into fire dragon and didnt have enough for a perfect defense. end of session 1 she lay dead impaled on a lunars spear as her soul was swallowed by oblivion.<br /> <br /> my most recent character is based on a combo of Hibiki Tachibana (Symphogear) and Azura (fire emblem fates) (maybe with a tad bit of valkyr from warframe) with an intent to be more or less the support-type zenith who can still blow up armies or smash things. that game died due to gm having life issues so ive been rewriting her to be better. (LFG btw)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1364,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1364-nemo_oceansoul","user":"Nemo_Oceansoul","date":". 04-15-2019, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1364-nemo_oceansoul","na